# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status {#check-the-status}"
msgstr "Verifique o status {#check-the-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Logo depois de chamar `run()`, o status geralmente é `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Meaning |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | The job waits for a compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | The workflow is starting an environment with the job's compute profile. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | The workflow's entrypoint is running. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | The entrypoint reported a stage with [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | You canceled the job, and the workflow is stopping it. |\n"
"| `DONE` | The entrypoint exited successfully. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | The entrypoint raised an error or exited with a nonzero code. See [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | You canceled the job, or it reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Significado |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | O job aguarda um slot de computação. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | O workflow está iniciando um ambiente com o perfil de computação do job. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | O ponto de entrada do workflow está em execução. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | O ponto de entrada reportou uma etapa com [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), como `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | Você cancelou o job e o workflow está interrompendo-o. |\n"
"| `DONE` | O ponto de entrada terminou com sucesso. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | O ponto de entrada gerou um erro ou terminou com código diferente de zero. Consulte [Encontre a causa de um erro](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | Você cancelou o job, ou ele atingiu o [limite de 24 horas](#time-limit). |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED` are final, and `job.in_terminal_state()` returns `True` for them. A status loop that waits for another value, such as `SUCCEEDED`, never ends.\n"
msgstr "`DONE`, `ERROR` e `CANCELED` são finais, e `job.in_terminal_state()` retorna `True` para eles. Um loop de status que espera outro valor, como `SUCCEEDED`, nunca termina.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wait for the job to end {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"
msgstr "Espere o job terminar {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To wait until the job ends, call `wait_for_final_state()`. It returns the final status, and with `verbose=True` it prints each status change. If you set `timeout` in seconds, `wait_for_final_state()` raises a `TimeoutError` when the time runs out before the job ends. The job keeps running:\n"
msgstr "Para esperar até o job terminar, chame `wait_for_final_state()`. Ele retorna o status final e, com `verbose=True`, imprime cada mudança de status. Se você definir `timeout` em segundos, `wait_for_final_state()` levanta um `TimeoutError` quando o tempo se esgota antes de o job terminar. O job continua em execução:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_for_final_state()` checks the status after 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 seconds, and then every 60 seconds, so it sees the end of a short job within seconds and makes few requests for a long job. To check at a fixed interval instead, pass `poll_interval` in seconds.\n"
msgstr "`wait_for_final_state()` verifica o status após 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 e 32 segundos, e depois a cada 60 segundos, de modo que percebe o fim de um job curto em poucos segundos e faz poucas requisições para um job longo. Para verificar em um intervalo fixo, passe `poll_interval` em segundos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the logs {#read-the-logs}"
msgstr "Leia os logs {#read-the-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. You can read them with `job.logs()` while the job runs, before it has a result:\n"
msgstr "Tudo o que o workflow escreve na saída padrão ou no erro padrão vai para os logs do job. Você pode lê-los com `job.logs()` enquanto o job executa, antes de ele ter um resultado:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow uploads new log lines about every 15 seconds, and one last time when the job ends or is canceled. Immediately after a job starts, `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.`\n"
msgstr "O workflow envia novas linhas de log aproximadamente a cada 15 segundos, e uma última vez quando o job termina ou é cancelado. Logo depois que um job começa, `job.logs()` retorna `No logs yet.`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow keeps the newest 50 MB of logs for each job, and adds a line at the top that says the logs were truncated.\n"
msgstr "O workflow mantém os 50 MB mais recentes de logs de cada job e adiciona uma linha no topo informando que os logs foram truncados.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To decide what your workflow logs, see [Write logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). To show only the lines that match a regular expression, pass `include` to `job.filtered_logs()`. To hide lines, pass `exclude`.\n"
msgstr "Para decidir o que seu workflow registra nos logs, consulte [Escreva logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). Para mostrar apenas as linhas que correspondem a uma expressão regular, passe `include` para `job.filtered_logs()`. Para ocultar linhas, passe `exclude`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the result {#get-the-result}"
msgstr "Obtenha o resultado {#get-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` espera até o job terminar e então retorna o valor que o workflow passou para [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, `job.result()` checks the status every 30 seconds and waits with no time limit. Pass `maxwait` to limit the number of checks. For example, `job.result(maxwait=40)` waits about 20 minutes. To check one time without waiting, pass `wait=False`. If `job.result()` stops waiting before the job ends, it returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Por padrão, `job.result()` verifica o status a cada 30 segundos e espera sem limite de tempo. Passe `maxwait` para limitar o número de verificações. Por exemplo, `job.result(maxwait=40)` espera cerca de 20 minutos. Para verificar uma única vez sem esperar, passe `wait=False`. Se `job.result()` parar de esperar antes de o job terminar, ele retorna `{}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check how long each stage took {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"
msgstr "Veja quanto tempo cada etapa levou {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events()` lists every status and stage change of a job with its time, so you can see how long the job waited for compute and how long each stage took:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.events()` lista toda mudança de status e de etapa de um job com seu horário, para que você veja quanto tempo o job esperou por computação e quanto tempo cada etapa levou:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The events use the stored status names. `PENDING` is `INITIALIZING`, and `SUCCEEDED` is `DONE`. For the QPU usage of a run, see [Find the QPU jobs of a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"
msgstr "Os eventos usam os nomes de status armazenados. `PENDING` é `INITIALIZING`, e `SUCCEEDED` é `DONE`. Para o uso de QPU de uma execução, consulte [Encontre os jobs de QPU de uma execução](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the cause of an error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"
msgstr "Encontre a causa de um erro {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status. For example, run the workflow with an angle that it rejects:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Quando o workflow levanta uma exceção, o job termina com o status `ERROR`. Por exemplo, execute o workflow com um ângulo que ele rejeita:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logs show the traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Os logs mostram o traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow [reports errors with `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), read them with `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, and read their messages with `job.error_message()`. For a job without reported errors, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns an empty list, and `job.error_message()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Se o workflow [reporta erros com `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), leia-os com `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` e leia suas mensagens com `job.error_message()`. Para um job sem erros reportados, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` retorna uma lista vazia, e `job.error_message()` retorna `{}`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: for custom workflows on Fleets, a raised ServerlessError is not recorded as an error event: only provider jobs run inside gateway/templates/main.tmpl, which calls send_error(). Custom jobs run the entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py. Confirm whether custom jobs should get the same handler, and whether error_message() should return a string instead of {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage jobs {#manage-jobs}"
msgstr "Gerencie jobs {#manage-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr "Cancele um job {#cancel-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cancel a job with `job.cancel()`. The status changes to `CANCELING` while the workflow stops the job, and then to `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Cancele um job com `job.cancel()`. O status muda para `CANCELING` enquanto o workflow interrompe o job e depois para `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message about the job and about its [linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), which it also tries to cancel. For a running job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint. To save partial results, see [Clean up when a job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). If the job already ended, `job.cancel()` returns `Job already in terminal state.` and changes nothing.\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` retorna uma mensagem sobre o job e sobre seus [jobs de QPU vinculados](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), que ele também tenta cancelar. Para um job em execução, o workflow envia `SIGTERM` ao seu ponto de entrada. Para salvar resultados parciais, consulte [Faça a limpeza quando um job for cancelado](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). Se o job já terminou, `job.cancel()` retorna `Job already in terminal state.` e não altera nada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: in a live test (1 Nov 2026), a job canceled while RUNNING went to CANCELING and then DONE, with its result saved, because the entrypoint finished before the stop took effect. Confirm whether a job that finishes during CANCELING should end as DONE or CANCELED. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a job from a new session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"
msgstr "Encontre um job a partir de uma nova sessão {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Job` object and the workflow exist only in your current Python session. After you restart a notebook kernel, pass the saved job ID to `client.job()`, or list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"O objeto `Job` e o workflow existem apenas na sua sessão atual do Python. Depois de reiniciar o kernel de um notebook, passe o ID do job salvo para `client.job()`, ou liste seus jobs recentes com `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`client.jobs()` returns your 10 most recent jobs, newest first. Filter it with `function`, `status` (from the [status table](#check-the-status)), or `created_after` (an ISO 8601 timestamp), and page through it with `limit` and `offset`. To list the workflows that you uploaded, call `client.list()`.\n"
msgstr "`client.jobs()` retorna seus 10 jobs mais recentes, do mais novo para o mais antigo. Filtre com `function`, `status` (da [tabela de status](#check-the-status)) ou `created_after` (um timestamp ISO 8601) e navegue pelas páginas com `limit` e `offset`. Para listar os workflows que você enviou, chame `client.list()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table on IBM Quantum Platform also lists your jobs, with their status, compute profile, and run times.\n"
msgstr "A tabela [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) na IBM Quantum Platform também lista seus jobs, com status, perfil de computação e tempos de execução.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time limit {#time-limit}"
msgstr "Limite de tempo {#time-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow cancels a job that runs for more than 24 hours, and the job ends with the `CANCELED` status. During long runs, [save checkpoints to file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) so that you do not lose work.\n"
msgstr "Um workflow gerenciado cancela um job que executa por mais de 24 horas, e o job termina com o status `CANCELED`. Durante execuções longas, [salve checkpoints no armazenamento de arquivos](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) para não perder trabalho.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the timeout is measured from the job's latest event, not from its start (gateway/scheduler/tasks/update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout). Calls to update_status() and send_error() create events, so a job that reports stages can run longer than 24 hours. This looks like a bug; confirm the intended behavior. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"
msgstr "Solucione problemas de jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Code: 429` and `Active job limit reached.` | You reached the [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Wait for some jobs to end, or [cancel](#cancel-a-job) jobs that you no longer need. |\n"
"| The job stays `QUEUED`, and `run()` warned that `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | The job does not start until the block on your account, plan, or subscription is lifted. Contact your administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.` | The job is queued or just started. Wait about 15 seconds. |\n"
"| `job.result()` returns `{}` | The job has not ended, was canceled, or saved no result. See [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` returns `{}` | The workflow raised an exception without reporting an error. Read the traceback with `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| The job is `CANCELED`, but you did not cancel it | The job reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Causa |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` falha com `Code: 429` e `Active job limit reached.` | Você atingiu o [limite de jobs ativos](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Espere alguns jobs terminarem ou [cancele](#cancel-a-job) jobs de que você não precisa mais. |\n"
"| O job permanece `QUEUED` e `run()` avisou `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | O job não começa até que o bloqueio na sua conta, plano ou assinatura seja removido. Entre em contato com seu administrador. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` retorna `No logs yet.` | O job está na fila ou acabou de começar. Espere cerca de 15 segundos. |\n"
"| `job.result()` retorna `{}` | O job não terminou, foi cancelado ou não salvou resultado. Consulte [Salve resultados](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` retorna `{}` | O workflow levantou uma exceção sem reportar um erro. Leia o traceback com `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| O job está `CANCELED`, mas você não o cancelou | O job atingiu o [limite de 24 horas](#time-limit). |\n"

